From 76ca2860f7641b8eea043eb35baa3d55a5ea5171 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Horizon authors <>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 00:07:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] World items and chests: ItemId, ITEM_NONE instead of 0xFF
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Step 3 of docs/mods/ids.md (§ 10), items outside the inventory.

- DROPPED_ITEMS and TAMER_ITEM (their type was already i32) mark a free
  slot with ITEM_NONE instead of 0xFF, so item 255 can lie on the ground.
- spawnItem, spawnDroppedItems, pickupItem, setItemTexture and
  renderItemSprite carry an ItemId; the four local renderItemSprite
  prototypes now agree with the definition.
- Chest.item is an ItemId (ITEM_NONE = no chest) in the byte and the
  padding byte after it, so the struct keeps its 56 bytes; spawnChest
  takes an ItemId and TAKE_CHEST_ITEM is an ItemId.
- SPAWN_ITEM and SPAWN_CHEST map their u8 item through itemFromLegacy.
- ITEM_NONE lives in ids.h next to ItemId.

The item icon grid still has 128 cells (ITEM.DAT, step 7).

